    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d696">

                <pb facs="0829" n="543" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg543"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/11342</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-24T19:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 24, 1917, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.45 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5537. Department’s 4117, December 2, 3 p. m., my 5290, December 7, 4 p. m., and
                    Department’s 4250, January 5, 4 p. m., <hi rendition="#italic">re</hi>
                    modification of instructions. Foreign Office informs me it has “decided to make
                    a special concession in regard to the two consignments.” British Consul,
                    Rotterdam, authorized to issue on application permits for shipment 10,000 bags
                    to DeRekowski and 10,215 bags Michigan Sugar Company.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
